  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\left\\{a_k\\right\\}$ and $\\left\\{b_k\\right\\}, k \\in \\mathbb{N}$, be two G.P.s with common ratio $r_1$ and $r_2$ respectively such that $\\mathrm{a}_1=\\mathrm{b}_1=4$ and $\\mathrm{r}_1&lt;\\mathrm{r}_2$. Let $\\mathrm{c}_{\\mathrm{k}}=\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{k}}+\\mathrm{b}_{\\mathrm{k}}, \\mathrm{k} \\in \\mathbb{N}$. If $\\mathrm{c}_2=5$ and $\\mathrm{c}_3=\\frac{13}{4}$ then $\\sum_{\\mathrm{k}=1}^{\\infty} \\mathrm{c}_{\\mathrm{k}}-\\left(12 \\mathrm{a}_6+8 \\mathrm{~b}_4\\right)$ is equal to"
  },
